<h2 id="worked-example">A worked example: April 2026</h2>

<p>This example uses the published decision for {{ latest.tax_year }} and the full new State Pension.</p>

<ol>
  <li>Prices rose by {{ latest.prices_tenths | percent }} in the year to September 2025.</li>
  <li>Earnings rose by {{ latest.earnings_tenths | percent }}, comparing May to July 2025 with a year earlier.</li>
  <li>The minimum is 2.5%.</li>
  <li>The highest is earnings, so the increase was {{ latest.applied_tenths | percent }}.</li>
  <li>{{ before.new_pence | money }} × {{ latest.applied_tenths | factor }} = {{ exNew.unroundedPence | pounds4 }}. Rounded to the nearest 5p, that is {{ latest.new_pence | money }} a week.</li>
  <li>The weekly increase was {{ (latest.new_pence - before.new_pence) | money }}.</li>
  <li>52 weeks at the new rate is {{ (latest.new_pence * 52) | money }}.</li>
</ol>
<p>{{ m.c("tl-2026-decision") }}</p>

<p>Rounding means the increase in pounds is not always exactly the headline percentage. In the same year the basic State Pension went from {{ before.basic_pence | money }} to {{ latest.basic_pence | money }}. The unrounded result was {{ exBasic.unroundedPence | pounds4 }}.</p>

